        "geology": "Eocene chalk bedrock, Miocene sediments (sandstone, sand, conglomerates), and Quaternary aeolian and alluvial sand/clay deposits.",
        "hydrology": "Ephemeral stream in wet season (winter); runoff flow on slopes due to low infiltration causes by biological soil crust, intercepted by mature shrub or grass vegetation.",
        "soils": "Serozem, depth 50-110 cm, color yellow/brown to reddish, texture sandy seine, at places with chalk and/or gypsum aggregates. The bulk soil has between 2 and 3% of carbon, a texture of 4% clay, 18% silt, 68% fine sand (b210 ?m) and 10% coarse sand, a pore volume of 0.46 and a bulk density of 1442 kg m?3. In some patches the soil is mixed with small rocky particles. ",
        "vegetation": "Semi-arid shrub-grassland slopes and hilltops dominated by Noaea mucronata and Atractylis serratuloides dwarf shrubs; Thylemaea hirsuta along ephemeral stream beds; Species-rich winter-annual vegetation (120 species), dominated by Stipa capensis."
